{
  "schema": 1,
  "note": "The canonical core vocabulary: the everyday words a learner is taught to name, as data. Hand-maintained source file - shared/stimuli/build.mjs reads it, nothing generates it. A word is {id, category, name, label, emoji}. `id` is the stable identity the whole library keys on and `name` is the file stem any art for it is stored under, so stimulusId(category, name) must equal id. `label` is what a learner-facing game prints: it wins over the label frozen in source-manifests.json and over the one derived from a filename, and loses only to a technician's own override in labels.json. `emoji` is the fallback drawn when no art exists yet - required for a word with no art, and explicitly null for a word that already ships a photograph and has no honest glyph in Unicode.",
